{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc","id":1125564,"title":"True Faith for each Paradigm/Tradition/etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-06T05:52:59-07:00","id":1125564,"title":"True Faith for each Paradigm/Tradition/etc.","content":"So I'm pretty fond of M20's True Faith. I think it does make Faith very powerful indeed, but it stays within the limits of what it should be capable of. Naturally True Faith makes the most sense with the Celestial Chorus (and those Disparates who behave like Knights Templar), but I was thinking about how Faith could be applied to the different types of Mage. True Faith of course cannot be an antagonist to your paradigm, and there has to be some synergy... any conflict would mean a low Arete at my table, which you could increase through seekings which reconcile the differences between your Faith and your Paradigm.<br /> <br /> For example, in the Cult of Ecstasy you could have a liberal Christian who believes in God-given tools. Conscience, pleasure, love, passion, these are all sacred gifts from God, and a large portion of Christianity is missing the point on this. Yes the union of a husband and wife in matrimony, conjugal love and children are all great, but it's too SPECIFIC a form of &quot;hedonism&quot; and it only works for some people. This Ecstatic believes in worshiping the wonderful things God has given us, and seeking &quot;inclusive hedonism&quot; as a form of ascension (people who are starving can't enjoy themselves, ergo we should do something about that). This would work well with Creation is Divine and alive, with Prayer, Meditation, Sex and Sensuality etc. Their Faith would be likely labelled as profane by many more conservative Christians, especially a Chorister. I could imagine them being deeply antagonized by the hedonistic &quot;you do you&quot; type being able to call upon divine aid.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for the other Traditions? How about the Conventions and the Disparates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-06-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:21:34-07:00","id":1125587,"title":"","content":"Remember, as much as it pains me to say so, True Faith in CWOD is not limited to the Christian Faith but includes any religion or belief that one holds strongly to. Therefore it can be applied to almost any Tradition or Convention no matter how bizzare their beliefs are.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons our group has mostly frowned upon the merit since the beginning of Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:41:07-07:00","id":1125593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125587#post1125587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, as much as it pains me to say so, True Faith in CWOD is not limited to the Christian Faith but includes any religion or belief that one holds strongly to. Therefore it can be applied to almost any Tradition or Convention no matter how bizzare their beliefs are.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons our group has mostly frowned upon the merit since the beginning of Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 says the belief must be sincere, and it must be a religious tradition with some temporal depth; no True Faith in post-modern concepts like the Flying Spaghetti Monster. True Faith in a fictional (one of the mythic NPCs in the WoD) or outdated (a religion which is practically speaking dead, like Roman Polytheism) deity? Cool! True Faith in any of the major world religions? Cool! ST can always say that a type of Faith isn't suited to their table; True Faith in Bulgroth the Unclean is certainly possible, even thematically appropriate, but it might not be good for your game.<br /> <br /> The question is how you make that system fit the different paradigms, if you want to do so. For example, I can't see any of the Abrahamic Religions and Hermetic Sorcery being perfect fits, however I'm sure there would be an interesting way of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-06-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:14:06-07:00","id":1125625,"title":"","content":"For an Iterator Character I have, he had True Faith in Humanity. Having essentially taken the disappearance of the Computer he had been raised to believe was an infallible god machine fairly hard, he redirected his faith towards the people who made it. Essentially taking the Anthropic Principle to it's logical conclusion and deciding that Humanity as a collective is a god that has lost it's way.<br /> <br /> Quite clearly, this lead to a rather militant stance towards any 'godlike' being that demanded worship. Clearly they were parasitic false deities siphoning off humanities own power and needed to be destroyed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:55:22-07:00","id":1125659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125625#post1125625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Iterator Character I have, he had True Faith in Humanity. Having essentially taken the disappearance of the Computer he had been raised to believe was an infallible god machine fairly hard, he redirected his faith towards the people who made it. Essentially taking the Anthropic Principle to it's logical conclusion and deciding that Humanity as a collective is a god that has lost it's way.<br /> <br /> Quite clearly, this lead to a rather militant stance towards any 'godlike' being that demanded worship. Clearly they were parasitic false deities siphoning off humanities own power and needed to be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how did other Technocrats feel about their Faith? How did it manifest? Surely miracles of True Faith, even a Humanitarian Faith, are reality deviance? Or did you just not use the deviant mechanics (laying hands to heal someone, warding evil) for TF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T12:15:34-07:00","id":1125662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125659#post1125659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So how did other Technocrats feel about their Faith? How did it manifest? Surely miracles of True Faith, even a Humanitarian Faith, are reality deviance? Or did you just not use the deviant mechanics (laying hands to heal someone, warding evil) for TF?</div> </div> </div> </div>I play Revised. The details of what sorts of 'Miracles' you can pull are essentially up to the ST and are basically down to &quot;You can perform a feat of appropriate magick without paradox.&quot;<br /> <br /> Normally it just provides +1 Willpower and a die of innate countermagick.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T12:26:27-07:00","id":1125664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125662#post1125662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I play Revised. The details of what sorts of 'Miracles' you can pull are essentially up to the ST and are basically down to &quot;You can perform a feat of appropriate magick without paradox.&quot;<br /> <br /> Normally it just provides +1 Willpower and a die of innate countermagick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well M20 goes a tad further.<br /> <br /> - +1 Willpower<br /> - 1 die of innate countermagic<br /> - A side-bar full of optional powers, such as Laying Hands to heal (or harm if your Faith is toxic), transmutations (water to wine, wine to blood), encouraging people to repent etc.<br /> - A description at each level with miscellaneous minor benefits, like people whose beliefs oppose your Faith (very strongly, serial killer types) feeling uncomfortable around you, higher difficulties to control you with Mind (or equivalent) etc. So a privileged aristocrat who had their pleasure at the expense of 1000s of poor people (like a Saudi Prince) would feel VERY uncomfortable around my Ecstatic, a violator of Human Rights would feel deeply uncomfortable around your Iterator...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:02:08-07:00","id":1125671,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Revised it's a 7-dot merit just to get 1 point of True Faith, and it's openly stated that getting more is nigh on impossible. And using it to perform blatant miracles can 'burn out' your faith if you begin to treat it like a tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:11:44-07:00","id":1125687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125671#post1125671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using it to perform blatant miracles can 'burn out' your faith if you begin to treat it like a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I think that on one hand you don't want it to be &quot;I use my True Faith to heal James's gunshot&quot; *mid-battle* since that's just &quot;I don't want to invest in Life 3 or deal with Paradox&quot;. Ideally it would be &quot;I lay hands on James's wound, and focus for a full minute while reflecting on the Archangel Raphael's salve&quot;, since there are sufficient downsides associated with this; you can't do it fast, you can't do it in turmoil, you can't do it to yourself, you can't do it for selfish reasons.<br /> <br /> So the ST does need to moderate it a tiny bit and reject abuse of it as the &quot;Faith Sphere&quot; basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T18:13:07-07:00","id":1125747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125625#post1125625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Iterator Character I have, he had True Faith in Humanity. Having essentially taken the disappearance of the Computer he had been raised to believe was an infallible god machine fairly hard, he redirected his faith towards the people who made it. Essentially taking the Anthropic Principle to it's logical conclusion and deciding that Humanity as a collective is a god that has lost it's way.<br /> <br /> Quite clearly, this lead to a rather militant stance towards any 'godlike' being that demanded worship. Clearly they were parasitic false deities siphoning off humanities own power and needed to be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just my recent obsession with Nier: Automata talking, but this would work especially well for an android character, whether Awakened or not. (You know, so long as the Storyteller is okay with an entirely artificial being having True Faith and/or True Magick). The android views humans in much the way humans view their own creator: with religious awe. The create life, alter the world around them to their will, etc.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glory to Mankind&quot; indeed. (I think I might create such an android character over in the 1001 Characters thread).<br /> <br /> I don't imagine the Technocracy would be too happy about some of their sapient robots actually developing a cult around them, but they might tolerate an informal devotion. One based on Laws passed down to the machines (from the Union itself, obviously), and that tolerates no superstitionist activities. The Union has a party line, here, so the worship of their human members by their machine ones must conform to the Enlightened, rational manner that is demanded of all its constituent parts. And so long as this devotion doesn't interfere with the efficient operation of Union business.<br /> <br /> A version of this informal Cult of Mankind could also be spread among the organic creations of the Progenitors. Helps to keep the Viktors from getting too full of themselves.<br /> <br /> Given all that, I would assume Technocratic True Faith would, by its very worldview, eschew overt miracles. Such things would be irrational, and therefore silly to expect. More subtle effects, though, would be possible. Finding an extra magazine of ammunition in a corner, or one's vehicle remaining running long after its systems should have failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:48:07-07:00","id":1125823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1125564-true-faith-for-each-paradigm-tradition-etc?p=1125747#post1125747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given all that, I would assume Technocratic True Faith would, by its very worldview, eschew overt miracles. Such things would be irrational, and therefore silly to expect. More subtle effects, though, would be possible. Finding an extra magazine of ammunition in a corner, or one's vehicle remaining running long after its systems should have failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;My designer would have forseen an eventuality such as me being given a massive dose of cyanide... I'm sure there's a subroutine for this in here SOMEWHERE&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm struggling to carry on, but I must. I have to carry out my duty&quot; - regains a point of Willpower -<br /> <br /> *Resists all attempts at mind control by a Nephandi; instinctively they can understand that this deviant's wishes are antithetical to existence itself, which runs contrary to its beliefs on a fundamental level*<br /> <br /> *Magic relying on the concept that all humans are fundamentally connected by some inherent &quot;Divinity&quot; can be coincidental*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}